      "id": "2093867375128945078",
      "text": "RT @teslaownersSV: Why Starship\n\nThe point of Starship is not that it is the biggest rocket.\nIt is that mass to orbit stops being a one-way…",
      "created_at": "Sun Aug 30 01:04:19 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2093767431861010813",
        "text": "Why Starship\n\nThe point of Starship is not that it is the biggest rocket.\nIt is that mass to orbit stops being a one-way ticket.\n\n@elonmusk \n“It's the first rocket design that is capable of full and rapid reusability.”\n\nTranslation: every other orbital rocket is still a disposable truck. Starship is built so the truck comes home and goes again. Refill is the next chapter. Reuse is the breakthrough.\n\n1. Falcon Heavy: ~64 t to LEO (expendable)\n2. Starship V3: >100 t to LEO reusable (SpaceX’s stated target)\n3. You cannot make enough rockets unless you can refly them\n4. Flight 13: Ship came home intact after entry\n\nYou cannot become multiplanetary on expendable trucks.",
        "created_at": "Sat Aug 29 18:27:10 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
